{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Seven years and seven years.</b> They are all only seven. And that the dream was repeated twice is because the matter is prepared — as he explained to him at the end: <b>and as for the doubling of the dream, etc.</b> Regarding the seven good years it says <b>he told Pharaoh</b>, because it was near; and regarding the seven years of famine it says <b>he showed Pharaoh</b>, because the matter was far-reaching and distant — the expression of showing applies to it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:56.921262155Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}